TI Polymer modified quartz tuning fork (QTF) sensor array for detection of breath as a biomarker for diabetes
SO SENSORS AND ACTUATORS B-CHEMICAL
LA English
DT Article
DE Quartz tuning fork; Sensor array; Volatile organic compounds; Breath Bio-markers; Diabetes; Neural networks
ID VOLATILE ORGANIC-COMPOUNDS; GAS SENSOR; TEMPERATURE; ACETONE; ISOPROPANOL; VAPOR
AB A sensor array of three polymer modified quartz tuning fork sensors has been developed to detect breath signature of health of three types of individuals, basal with no history of diabetes, self-declared diabetic individuals and individuals with more than average physical activity labeled as individuals with high metabolic rate (HMR). Breath samples were collected from 70 individuals and sensor array output of more than 2200 exposures was collected. Sensor was initially tested for various analytes for its selectivity and then Neural network was trained using sensor response to acetone and breath samples from all three categories. Sensor response in terms of shift in resonant frequency of the quartz tuning fork sensors, response time and rate and recovery time and rate were used as input features to design a multi-layered neural network to predict the health state of the participants with similar to 95% accuracy. Individuals with basal state and diabetes states could be identified with better accuracy compared to individuals with HMR state. Further improvement in sensor array as well as training of neural network can lead to a simple and cheap device to monitor metabolic rate non-invasively.
