PT J
AU Maffi, JM
   Sosa, J
   Estenoz, DA
AF Maffi, J. M.
   Sosa, J.
   Estenoz, D. A.
TI Development of hybrid (AI/first principle) models for the optimization of styrene polymerization processes
SO CHEMICAL ENGINEERING SCIENCE
LA English
DT Article
ID POLYSTYRENE
AB In this work, two mathematical modelling strategies are developed to predict the behavior of a standard polystyrene industrial plant: a kinetic polymerization model derived from first principles, and a black -box neural network. Both general purpose polystyrene (GPPS) and high -impact polystyrene (HIPS) plants are evaluated, considering the reaction trains and the post-reaction devolatizer (DV). Each model is adjusted to fit industrial data, and their performance is assessed in terms of prediction accuracy and run time. Results show that the traditional polymerization model may be improved if the DV module is replaced with a trained neural network, resulting in a hybrid model with a very good performance. Finally, a theoretical model is built using a second neural network, but trained with a very large dataset, produced with the adjusted hybrid model. This provides a very fast model that can be used in optimization routines to look for tailor-made grades.
