TI Protocol for creating representations of molecular structures using a polymer-specific decoder
SO STAR PROTOCOLS
LA English
DT Article
AB To supply chemical structures of polymers for machine learning applications, decoding is necessary. Here, we present a protocol for generating polymer fingerprints (PFPs), which are representations of molecular structures, using a polymer -specific decoder. We outline steps for downloading, installing, and basic application of the software. Moreover, we present procedures for processing and analyzing polymer structure data and the preparation for integration into machine learning methods. On this basis, we explain how artificial neural networks can be utilized to predict polymer properties. For complete details on the use and execution of this protocol, please refer to Ko<spacing diaeresis> ster et al. 1
