TI A hybrid GMDH neural network to investigate partition coefficients of Penicillin G Acylase in polymer-salt aqueous two-phase systems
SO JOURNAL OF MOLECULAR LIQUIDS
LA English
DT Article
DE Partitioning; Aqueous two-phase systems; GMDH; Neural network
ID POLY(ETHYLENE GLYCOL); PROTEIN PARTITION; SODIUM-CITRATE; AMINO-ACIDS; BIOMOLECULES; MODEL; PREDICTION; PHOSPHATE
AB To model partition coefficients of Penicillin G Acylase in polymer-salt aqueous two-phase systems (ATPS), a hybrid GMDH neural network is presented on the basis of original GMDH approach. We performed two major amendments to the structure of original approach in order to enhance the model complexity and power to trace high order of non-linearity. An extensive data set observed by Pazuki et al. is examined by original GMDH approach and hybrid GMDH neural network model. Compared to results generated by original GMDH approach and UNIFAC-FV model, hybrid model stands out with a noticeable superiority in tracking data trend. Average Absolute Deviation percent (AAD%) of proposed hybrid model is 4.04% which indicates a superior accuracy in comparison with those of original GMDH approach and UNIFAC-FV model with AADs% of 6.91% and 5.58%. Crown Copyright (C) 2013 Published by Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.
