TI The effects of morphological variation and polymer/polymer interface on the tensile modulus of binary polymer blends: a modeling approach
SO JOURNAL OF POLYMER ENGINEERING
LA English
DT Article
DE analytical modeling; artificial neural network systems; binary polymer blends; Kolarik's model; mechanical properties; tensile modulus
ID MECHANICAL-PROPERTIES; JANUS NANOPARTICLES; SIMULTANEOUS PREDICTION; YIELD STRENGTH; NANOCOMPOSITES; APPROXIMATION; SYSTEMS; FIBER
AB In this work, the effects of the morphological variation and the polymer/polymer interface on the tensile modulus of binary polymer blends were evaluated using a combined modeling method. The characteristics of the polymer/polymer interface region were evaluated using a neural network system and the results were used to improve the analytical model. The model accuracy was investigated by comparing its predictions with the tensile test results of some prepared iPP/PA blend samples and also some other data from literature which revealed an acceptable accuracy (error < 5%).
