TI Blister Defect Detection Based on Convolutional Neural Network for Polymer Lithium-Ion Battery
SO APPLIED SCIENCES-BASEL
LA English
DT Article
DE defect detection; polymer lithium-ion battery; convolutional neural network; deep learning; blister defect; flower pollination algorithm
ID FLOWER POLLINATION ALGORITHM; SOLID-ELECTROLYTE INTERPHASE; TEMPERATURE DISTRIBUTIONS; CLASSIFICATION; SIMULATION; INSPECTION; DIAGNOSIS; DATASET; DESIGN; MODEL
AB To ensure the quality and reliability of polymer lithium-ion battery (PLB), automatic blister defect detection instead of manual detection is developed in the production of PLB cell sheets. A convolutional neural network (CNN) based detection method is proposed to detect blister in cell sheets employing cell sheet images. An improved architecture for dense block and a learning method based on optimization of learning rate are discussed. The proposed method was superior to other machine learning based methods when the classification performance and confusion matrix were compared in experiments. The proposed CNN method had the best defect detection performance and real-time performance for industry field application.
