TI Predicting mechanical properties of elastomeric modified nylon blend using adaptive neuro-fuzzy interference system and neural network
SO INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF ADVANCED MANUFACTURING TECHNOLOGY
LA English
DT Article
DE ANFIS; ANN; Blend; Mechanical properties; Polyamide-6
ID RULES
AB Artificial neural network (ANN) and adaptive neuro-fuzzy inference system (ANFIS) are employed to predict the final mechanical properties of Polyamide 6 (PA6)/ ethylene-propylene-rubber (EPR)-grafted blend at different compositions. An individual ANFIS model is developed to predict the mechanical property at different processing condition. The results of this study are suggestive that both ANFIS and ANN could be employed quite effectively for this aim in such a polymer blend system. Therefore, the mechanical properties such as yield strength, modulus, and Izod impact strength are well predicted employing this method including an acceptable range of errors.
