TI High-precision MoS2/PVA polymer electret synaptic transistors for neuromorphic computations
SO SENSORS AND ACTUATORS A-PHYSICAL
LA English
DT Article
DE Polymer electret film; Synaptic transistors; Image recognition; MoS2/PVA
ID FIELD-EFFECT TRANSISTORS; NANOSHEETS
AB Polymer electret synaptic transistors are a promising type of three-terminal artificial synaptic device. In this work, the morphological structure and dielectric properties of MoS2/PVA composite films with different MoS2 concentrations were studied, and it was determined that the MoS2/PVA composite film with a MoS2 concentration of 0.6 mg mL-1 is the polymer electret insulating layer with the optimal performance. Subsequently, it was combined with a semiconductor thin film at a low temperature to construct a MoS2/PVA thin film transistor with good performance. The MoS2/PVA polymer electret synaptic transistor exhibits typical synaptic characteristics, including short-term plasticity (STP), long-term plasticity (LTP) and paired pulse facilitation (PPF). Besides, repeated continuous potentiation and depression (PD) pulse groups were applied on the synaptic transistor and good stability, uniformity, and linearity of the synaptic transistor were proved. Based on the PD characteristic data triggered by 35 pulse groups obtained in the experiment, using a three-layer artificial neural network to train and test the image recognition capability of the synaptic transistor on the CrossSim platform. The device shows the high image recognition accuracy of 93.8 % for the MNIST dataset. Thus, the MoS2/PVA polymer electret synaptic transistor is expected to become a potential candidate for neuromorphic computations and electronic skin.
