TI Deep-learning-assisted inverse modelling of magnetorheological elastomer tuned mass damper for vibration control of offshore wind turbines
SO OCEAN ENGINEERING
LA English
DT Article
DE Semi-active control; Deep learning model; Magnetorheological elastomer; Offshore wind turbine
ID SEMIACTIVE CONTROL
AB With the rapid expansion of offshore wind energy, monopile offshore wind turbines (MOWTs) are increasingly exposed to severe vibration problems induced by coupled wind-wave excitations, which threaten structural safety and serviceability. This study proposes a novel semi-active vibration mitigation framework for MOWTs by integrating a variable-stiffness magnetorheological elastomer tuned mass damper (MRE-TMD) with semi-active control empowered by deep-learning-assisted inverse modelling. A 1:70 scaled experimental MOWT model is developed based on similarity theory, and equivalent combined wind-wave loadings are reproduced through shaking-table excitation. A prototype MRE-TMD is designed and fabricated, and its wide-range, field-dependent stiffness tunability is experimentally validated. To address the strongly nonlinear and hysteretic inverse dynamics of the MRE-TMD, a convolutional neural network-bidirectional long short-term memory-attention (CBA) inverse model is established to accurately map the relationship between the desired control force and the required actuation current. The inverse model is embedded within a semi-active control framework in conjunction with a linear quadratic regulator (LQR), enabling real-time stiffness tuning of the MRE-TMD. Shaking-table experiments demonstrate that the proposed CBA-LQR-controlled MRE-TMD reduces the towertop displacement peak and RMS by up to 66.9% and 68.6%, respectively, compared with the uncontrolled case. Moreover, it significantly outperforms conventional passive control, achieving additional reductions of up to 63.2% in peak displacement and 47.2% in RMS response. The results confirm that the proposed deep-learningassisted semi-active MRE-TMD provides effective vibration suppression with effective control action, offering a promising and practical solution for vibration mitigation of offshore wind turbines operating in harsh marine environments.
